\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord God, by whom all change is wrought,
\par By whom new things to birth are brought,
\par In whom no change is known;
\par Whate'er Thou dost, whate'er Thou art,
\par Thy people still in Thee have part,
\par Still, still Thou art our own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ancient of Days, we dwell in Thee;
\par Out of Thine own eternity
\par Our peace and joy are wrought;
\par We rest in our eternal God,
\par And make secure and sweet abode
\par With Thee, who changest not.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Spirit who makest all things new,
\par Thou leadest onward; we pursue
\par The heavenly march sublime.
\par 'Neath Thy renewing fire we glow,
\par And still from strength to strength we go,
\par From height to height we climb.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Darkness and dread we leave behind;
\par New light, new glory still we find,
\par New realms divine possess;
\par New births of grace, new raptures bring;
\par Triumphant, the new song we sing,
\par The great Renewer bless.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. To Thee we rise, in Thee we rest;
\par We stay at home, we go in quest,
\par Still Thou art our abode.
\par The rapture swells, the wonder grows,
\par As full on us new life still flows
\par From our unchanging God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

